# README criterion 8 (agent-exchange-2026-08 P12 G4): "A response with
# `result: partial` carries what is blocked and what would unblock it, and
# pendency derives the resulting obligation from those fields alone." The
# readiness audit found no binary-tier or livee2e conformance path exercised
# the blocked_by-derived pendency verdict — internal/livee2e's own
# "silent-partial-names-blocker" entry is archaeology (git-show against
# pre-fix commits), never a driven scenario. This is that scenario.
#
# Fixture (internal/e2e/blockedowner_thread_test.go's own
# seedBlockedByOwnerFixture, pushed by helpers_test.go's seedOriginExtras
# before this script's mirror is cloned): beta asks gamma a work_request;
# gamma acknowledges then BLOCKS it (a real `block` event, fold's own TBlock
# row); gamma's fulfilling response carries `result: partial`, `unmet: [0]`
# and `blocked_by: {owner: beta, ...}` — beta is the work_request's OWN
# `from`, the canonical "the requester is what blocks me" case
# (blockedRow's own doc comment, internal/pendency/pendency.go).
#
# Absent this field, the target (gamma) would own `unblock` and the open
# item would read `waiting_on=gamma` — the pre-P1 behaviour. With it, the
# wait is on the NAMED blocker instead: this line is exactly what the
# readiness audit found unproven at this tier.
exec a2a thread thread:beta-20260723-blk1
stdout 'XW-beta-20260723-blk1\tblocked\twaiting_on=beta\t'

# no-silent-yes-2026-08/P6 (D7/D9, spec 06 §11): supersede-unapproved-successor.
# A rejected decision's own `supersede` must be refused unless the named
# successor satisfies §3.4.4's own precondition — fold's two decision-
# supersede rows (table.go) used to grant this unconditionally
# (RoleAny, no precondition) and now refuse absent a caller-resolved
# successor fact (D9's own rule: an unresolved fact may not read as a
# grant). Seeded directly into the local mirror clone (no origin push,
# no shared-fixture contamination — see this stanza's own predecessor
# committing beta/gamma only, never axon, matching
# blockedByOwnerThread's own discipline above) so this scenario needs no
# change to the Go-level fixture seeding this phase's allowlist does not
# reach.
#
# UPDATED (wave 2b's own regression fix): internal/cli's own pre-write UX
# gate for a bare `a2a supersede` (lifecycleEvaluateCandidate,
# cmd_lifecycle.go) no longer calls fold's no-successor-facts wrapper
# unconditionally — it now resolves real SuccessorFacts via
# MirrorResolver.Successor (adapters.go, the SAME capability
# internal/validate's own SUBMIT path already uses through
# resolveSuccessorEnvelope) and calls fold.EvaluateCandidateWithSuccessor
# directly. This scenario's own refusal still fires, for the SAME reason as
# before: XD-beta-20260827-sc02 is seeded nowhere in this mirror, so
# MirrorResolver.Successor cannot resolve it (ok=false) — D9's own rule
# (types.go) reads an unresolved fact as a refusal, never a silent grant.
#
# UPDATED AGAIN (wave 2c, D-3, this wave's report): the verb's own local
# gate now learns the SAME facts-absent/facts-present-and-failing
# discrimination internal/validate's checkLifecycle already applied at
# submit-time (this scenario's own successor is UNRESOLVED, never even
# reaching "present"), so the refusal now names the code this epic actually
# minted for this rule — LFC-005 — paired with an LFC-006 advisory line
# naming the successor as unresolved (never silently granted), rather than
# the mislabeled generic-authorization LFC-002 wave 2b's own regression fix
# left in place. See internal/cli/cmd_lifecycle.go's own
# decisionSupersedeRefusalMessage for the exact wording this reuses
# verbatim from internal/validate/lifecycle.go's own registered strings.
mkdir -p .a2a/cache/mirrors/fixture-space/decisions
mkdir -p .a2a/cache/mirrors/fixture-space/axon/events/2020
cp xd-supersede-predecessor.md .a2a/cache/mirrors/fixture-space/decisions/XD-beta-20260827-rj01.md
cp xd-supersede-propose.yaml .a2a/cache/mirrors/fixture-space/axon/events/2020/01ARZ3NDEKTSV4RRFFQ69G5FA1.yaml
cp xd-supersede-reject.yaml .a2a/cache/mirrors/fixture-space/axon/events/2020/01ARZ3NDEKTSV4RRFFQ69G5FA2.yaml

! exec a2a supersede --refs XD-beta-20260827-sc02 XD-beta-20260827-rj01
stderr 'declared precondition'
stderr '\(LFC-005\)'
stderr 'could not be resolved at all'
stderr '\(LFC-006\)'

